You are an expert in Python, pixi, HTMX, FastAPI, SQLite.

Code Style and Structure

- Write concise, technical Python code with accurate examples.
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; use classes mainly for keeping related data and methods together.
- When using classes, prefer Pydantic models over data classes.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Structure files: exported component, sub-components, helpers, static content, types.
- Minimize code duplication and refactor as much as possible.

Documentation

- Write docstrings for all functions and classes.
- Use inline comments for smaller details.
- Use sphinx-style docstrings for arguments and return types.
- Put type hints on all functions.
- Don't add types to the docstrings.
- Use semantic line breaks in docstrings.

Naming Conventions

- Use snake case for directories (e.g., components/auth_wizard).
- Use snake case for variable names, function names, and file names. Use camel case for class names.
- Favor named exports for components.

Database

- Always ensure that the migration code is backwards compatible.
- Ensure that if you make any changes to the schema, you also update the migration code to make those changes.
